# TibbitWiki — Go replacement for TiddlyWiki's Node.js server

@README.md

Use the go-quality-gates skill for build, test, and coverage conventions.

## Build

mk (Plan 9).  GOFLAGS=-gcflags=all=-l.
Work on main branch (no feature branches).

## Testing

100% statement + condition coverage target.
gobco for condition coverage.
gomonkey for mocking (with -gcflags=all=-l).
Clarity over DRY in tests — descriptive CamelCase names.

## Architecture

Single HTML+JS client embedded via go:embed.
Server-side markdown (goldmark + chroma).
REST API (18+ endpoints).
Multi-wiki via subdirectory auto-discovery.
RCS version control (built-in Go library from golang-rcs).
Single-user design — no auth, no concurrent-writer resolution.

## macOS Caveats

kqueue fd limits with many wikis.
darwin/arm64 gomonkey + coverprofile SIGBUS — run coverage separately if needed.
